{"kind":"propose","text":"Adopt, complete and exact, the landing-obligation design recorded in notes/2026-09-04-landing-obligation.md at candidate head 83eb0e6f9c05900b08b7c116a6f0f3d7445e7110 (artifact dd6adfdd, one commit on main d09a5a8d). This proposal rests on that artifact alone and re-adopts the whole note on its own authority; it inherits nothing from scope proposal #16918, which is named here only as history: hugh ratified it before this note existed and it is now stale. What ratification adopts: every state@3 request states its result as a full target triple into a refs/heads branch, target=inherit, or no_git_artifact=true; a landing request closes only by a sealed receipt into its target or by carried-or-abandoned supersession, no report completes it, and a resolution report is nonterminal evidence; one bounded deterministic inheritance rule that refuses conflicts; a hold released only by a structured authorization signed by exactly the hold owner the request author named, which narrows the current signer list for held requests; unheld landings sealing no authorization and released holds sealing theirs; receipts bound to the target; target-relative approved_not_landed on every surface; a narrow tested transfer-staleness exception; awaiting-review, awaiting-authorization and awaiting-landing replacing awaiting-merge at every named site; workroom-fold@19 with state@3 schema-keyed admission; and the I1 to I6 and W1 follow-on requests with their acceptance tests. It authorizes no production implementation; each follow-on request is filed and satisfied on its own. A fresh independent review request will rest on this proposal and artifact dd6adfdd once ratified. Replaces proposal 7b26d07e, which was stale at birth.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:dd6adfdd55ad549b4a2a701f7cf91861e8e466d9","head":"83eb0e6f9c05900b08b7c116a6f0f3d7445e7110","path":"notes/2026-09-04-landing-obligation.md"}}